    "description": "Waterman\nMarbled Black Fountain Pen\nLaureat II, Late 20th Century\nThe Waterman Laureat II is a classic writing instrument known for its distinctive ribbed grip and elegant proportions. This example features a marbled black finish with rich gold-tone accents, embodying the sophisticated French design Waterman is celebrated for. Produced in France, the Laureat series remains a favorite among collectors for its reliable performance and balanced feel in the hand.\nWaterman France gold-tone nib\nMarbled black resin body with gold-tone clip and decorative rings\nSignature ribbed black section for enhanced grip\nSnap-fit cap design with Waterman branding on the clip\nCondition:\nGood vintage condition. The body and cap show light surface wear and minor scuffing consistent with age and handling. Gold-tone trim remains bright. The nib is physically intact but shows dried ink residue; the pen is untested for ink flow or internal filling mechanism function.\nPayment Extensions -\nDue to demand, we will no longer extend any payment deadlines.\nAuthenticated Items Returns & Refund Disclaimer -\nRefunds and returns must be inquired on within 7 days of receipt of item(s). Returns on authenticated items will be refunded the amount paid for the item (excluding shipping and handling) less a restocking fee.\nCustomer Service -\nCustomer messages are processed Monday through Friday between 7:00am to 3:00 pm EST. We strive to respond to all customer messages within 48 hours.  Inquiries about auctions ending in less than 24 hours may not be answered before the end of the auction.",
